p="An online food-ordering company sends each new order to an Amazon SQS standard queue that is consumed by a kitchen-dispatch service. Customers are allowed to cancel an order within 5 minutes of placing it, so no order should become visible to the dispatch service until 5 minutes after it is sent. Cancellation is handled by a separate process. The company wants the simplest solution that does not require changes to the consumer code. Which solution meets these requirements?",
o=["Set the visibility timeout of the queue to 5 minutes so that messages are hidden from the dispatch service for that period.",
   "Add a sleep of 5 minutes in the dispatch service after it receives each message and before it processes the order.",
   "Configure the queue as a delay queue by setting its delivery delay (DelaySeconds) to 300 seconds.",
   "Set the message retention period of the queue to 5 minutes so that orders are kept for the cancellation window."],
c="C",
