# 8 KDS poison record multi - Select TWO (B, E)
Q.append(dict(t="2.1", tp=["Amazon Kinesis Data Streams", "AWS Lambda", "Event source mapping"],
p="An AWS Lambda function processes records from an Amazon Kinesis Data Streams stream through an event source mapping. Occasionally a malformed record causes the function to throw an exception. When this happens, the same batch is retried repeatedly and processing of that shard stops until the record expires, which delays all later records. The company wants healthy records to continue to be processed and wants to keep details of failed records for investigation. Which combination of actions will meet these requirements? (Select TWO.)",
o=["Increase the data retention period of the stream to 365 days.",
   "Enable BisectBatchOnFunctionError on the event source mapping.",
   "Configure a dead-letter queue in the Lambda function's asynchronous invocation settings.",
   "Increase the parallelization factor of the event source mapping to 10.",
   "Set MaximumRetryAttempts on the event source mapping and configure an on-failure destination such as an Amazon SQS queue."],
c="BE",
w=[("Bisect on error (B)", "Splitting a failed batch in half and retrying each half isolates the malformed record, so the healthy records in the batch are processed."),
   ("Bounded retries + on-failure destination (E)", "Limiting retries stops the shard from being blocked indefinitely, and the on-failure destination receives metadata about the discarded batch (shard, sequence numbers) for investigation."),
   ("Together", "Bisecting narrows the failure to the bad record, and bounded retries let the shard move past it.")],
x={"A": "Longer retention only means the blocking record would be retried for longer; it makes the problem worse.",
   "C": "Asynchronous-invocation dead-letter queues do not apply to stream event source mappings, which invoke the function synchronously.",
   "D": "A higher parallelization factor processes more batches concurrently per shard, but records with the same partition key still wait behind the failing record."},
e=[("Poison records in Kinesis/DynamoDB Streams with Lambda", "BisectBatchOnFunctionError + MaximumRetryAttempts/MaximumRecordAgeInSeconds + on-failure destination."),
   ("SQS vs stream sources", "SQS sources use a redrive policy DLQ on the queue; stream sources use on-failure destinations on the event source mapping.")]))
